└── async concurrency runtime for Socket.IO server
    ├── Candidates : eventlet, gevent
    ├── Used APIs  : monkey_patch
    ├── Pitfalls   : gevent uses a different hub implementation; some C extensions that 
    │   work with eventlet may block the gevent loop; eventlet's tpool (thread pool) API 
    │   has no direct equivalent in gevent — any explicit tpool usage would need rewriting;
    │   websocket performance characteristics differ; load-test before switching in 
    │   production
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── eventlet.monkey_patch() is called to enable cooperative multitasking for the 
        Flask-SocketIO server. gevent is the only other mature greenlet-based runtime that 
        Flask-SocketIO officially supports as a drop-in replacement; both provide 
        monkey-patching and a WSGI server compatible with socketio.run().

