    ├── Used APIs  : AES.new, AES.MODE_CBC, encrypt, decrypt
    ├── Pitfalls   : PyCrypto's AES.new accepts key/IV as str/bytes interchangeably; 
    │   cryptography requires bytes explicitly; cryptography uses separate 
    │   Cipher/encryptor/decryptor objects instead of a single object with encrypt/decrypt 
    │   methods; cryptography does not implement null-byte padding automatically — must be 
    │   handled manually or via PKCS7 padding; pycryptodome is API-compatible with PyCrypto
    │   but inherits same padding/IV handling quirks; Fixed IV (b'0000000000000000') is a 
    │   security anti-pattern; migration is opportunity to use random IVs
    ├── Constraints: crypto_required, requires_connector
    └── The code uses PyCrypto's AES implementation in CBC mode with a fixed IV and 
        null-byte padding. Both 'cryptography' (via hazmat.primitives.ciphers) and 
        'pycryptodome' (drop-in replacement for PyCrypto) provide equivalent AES-CBC 
        functionality. PyCrypto is unmaintained and has known HIGH-severity CVEs 
        (GHSA-6528-wvf6-f6qg, GHSA-cq27-v7xp-c356), making migration strongly advisable.

